From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:56:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_DEBUG=fault times encoders on the phone, names
 vertex stages that write a layer, and can leave draws out

The second phone repro of The Witcher 3 1.32's GPU hang (PLA-880) printed
no encoder timestamps: the counter heap 0156 asked for had 8192 entries,
and the phone refuses more than 4096 ("Requested Heap size is too large
(requested 8192 max is 4096)"). The heap now has KK_TS_HEAP_ENTRIES (4096,
the query pools' limit), so 2048 encoders, and a failed commit says where
the GPU stopped: "cb #N stopped in enc i" (started, not ended), "stopped
after enc i ... enc i+1 did not start", or that no encoder wrote one.

The failed command buffer held, after the game's G-buffer passes, a 5-layer
64x64 RGBA32F pass and a 5-layer 1024x1024 RG16F pass of one 4-vertex draw
each, then one pass per other layer of each image with the same pipeline,
then 5 instances into a single-layer R8 target. A vertex stage that writes
a layer at or past the pass's layers is undefined in Vulkan and Metal
(Direct3D uses layer 0). With MESA_KK_DEBUG=fault:
- the trail marks each pipeline whose hardware vertex stage writes a layer
  or viewport index (msl=...xN[layer]), and the first draw of such a
  pipeline in a pass of each layer count is logged once ("msl=X writes
  [layer]: drawn in a pass of L layer(s) WxH, xI instance(s)"), so a run
  shows whether the game draws one into fewer layers than it may write;
- MESA_KK_FAULT_SKIP=<MSL hash prefix>,...,layer,viewport (the game's
  Graphics options) leaves out the draws of those pipelines, counted as
  skipped=N in the trail and the encoder label, so one run can test
  whether they are what hangs.

MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=layer_clamp (off by default, in the pipeline cache
UUID when on) makes a hardware vertex stage write layer 0 for a layer at or
past the render pass's layers, as Direct3D does: a new system value,
render_target_layers_kk, read from the root table, which each
vkCmdBeginRendering sets to Metal's renderTargetArrayLength (1 without
attachments).

Linear: PLA-880
Class: diagnostics
Evidence: build/mesa-host-test/kk-fault-test.c (mock Metal refusing a heap over 4096 entries; layered blits; skips; a stop between encoders), kk-host-test.c "ok layer layer_clamp" (layer.vert); PLA-880 (phone2 repro: timestamps "(none)")
Offered-upstream: no
